Cases for the effects of each core op instance, shared by two tests:
`lean/FirTest/EffectCases.lean` and `crates/funk-ir/tests/effects.rs`.
Each case starts with a line of three equals signs, its name and the
effects of the op it pins: the first op of the entry block of `@f`. The
effects are `pure`, or a comma-separated list in this order: `reads(M)`,
`writes(M)`, `allocates(M)`, `may-ub`, `may-poison`, `observable` and
`control`, where `M` is `*` for every memory, or the memories joined by `+`.
The cases cover every core op, each flag set of `add`, `sub` and `mul`, and
`exact` on `sdiv` and `udiv`: the attributes that change an op's set.

=== const pure
func @f(%a: i8, %b: i8, %c: i1) -> i8 {
^entry:
  %r: i8 = const 1 @0
  ret %r @0
}

locs {
  @0 = unknown
}

